# What the mastodon form, booted as it ships, without a shell and without
# a config, must say on its console (make check-shellfree-mastodon;
# test/boot; forms/demo/test/console has the format). The streaming
# server starts on its leash and listens on loopback. The web, given no
# owner, parks before anything is made or served, and says why; the jobs,
# cron and nginx wait for what its first start makes. Nothing else fails.
# make check-mastodon boots it with its config, and checks it serves.

seen    stream-leashed    leash: \{"event":"start","service":"mastodon-streaming","user":"mastodon-stream"
seen    stream-listening  Streaming API now listening on 127\.0\.0\.1:4000
seen    web-needs-owner   leash: \{"event":"down","service":"mastodon","why":"config owner-password: FileNotFound"\}
unseen  others-down       leash: \{"event":"down","service":"(mastodon-streaming|mastodon-jobs|cron|nginx|postgres|valkey)"
unseen  secrets-made      mastodon: made the secrets
